WEBVTT

00:04.560 --> 00:05.690
Why just curry?

00:04.810 --> 00:06.770
is pork curry

00:04.810 --> 00:04.850
   The only item
on the menu
today is pork curry

00:05.690 --> 00:06.770
That's pushing it.

00:06.770 --> 00:08.440
Nothing we can do about it.

00:08.440 --> 00:10.360
The higher-ups told us to.

00:10.360 --> 00:13.660
Well, that's fine. It's still tasty.

00:14.570 --> 00:17.660
It's been getting pretty dangerous lately.

00:17.660 --> 00:22.330
I heard that Corpse showed up pretty close, so of course there'd be fewer people.

00:23.290 --> 00:25.670
Hey, Akashi, aren't you going to eat?

00:25.670 --> 00:27.460
Y-Yeah...

00:29.250 --> 00:33.170
Yoshida and Kagemori are gonna move away after all.

00:33.170 --> 00:34.630
<i>What does it all mean?</i>

00:35.340 --> 00:36.090
That moment...

00:36.720 --> 00:40.390
The usual disgusting feeling was gone for an instant.

00:40.600 --> 00:43.890
Was that thing resonating with the Reaper?

00:56.160 --> 00:56.200
The Dark Metal

01:01.700 --> 01:06.120
Night turns to day, and day turns to night. Our wishes have wilted away

01:06.120 --> 01:10.300
Where did the person I want to meet go?

01:10.300 --> 01:14.760
Interlocking these fingers with my beloved

01:14.760 --> 01:18.510
Even though I can't feel them, I continue to live

01:18.550 --> 01:23.140
When the flower's petals

01:23.140 --> 01:27.270
Are plucked off by the wind's playful gale

01:27.270 --> 01:31.730
They are scattered in every direction

01:31.730 --> 01:37.070
Even if you long for it

01:38.070 --> 01:42.790
Don't disappear, just don't

01:42.790 --> 01:46.580
I can even give everything else away if I have to

01:46.580 --> 01:51.420
You were there, and I was there with you

01:51.420 --> 01:55.760
Let me take in these memories

01:55.760 --> 02:02.680
These brief moments are connected, turning it into eternity

02:19.490 --> 02:22.700
Episode 7
Command of Solitude

02:20.700 --> 02:23.030
First, I'd like you to explain yourself, Natsuiri.

02:23.410 --> 02:28.210
If Corpses, which are are supposed to be bound to the Lightless Realm, can just freely leave,

02:28.210 --> 02:30.120
then we need to come up with
countermeasures against them.

02:30.500 --> 02:37.170
The Lightless Realm is shrouded in mystery, so anything that happens out of the ordinary isn't so surprising, right?

02:37.170 --> 02:40.300
That's why we need to investigate.

02:40.300 --> 02:43.850
Then you can start investigating immediately?

02:43.850 --> 02:48.600
The second MA-Vess created based on the Argent is already complete.

02:48.600 --> 02:51.940
All we need to do now is find a suitable pilot for it.

02:51.940 --> 02:54.610
You already found one pilot.

02:54.610 --> 02:56.860
Why not send that one to investigate alone?

02:56.860 --> 02:58.530
Please hold on!

02:58.530 --> 03:03.450
Are you saying you've already forgotten about what happened to the lone prototype Argent

03:03.450 --> 03:05.200
that went in for secondary investigations?

03:05.200 --> 03:08.830
The Lightless Realm's invasion of
the human psyche and the machine

03:08.830 --> 03:11.460
with a mental stimulation module to withstand it.

03:12.130 --> 03:16.250
That's what the Shirogane,
the prototype for the Argent, was.

03:16.920 --> 03:21.760
However, the fate of the
pilot who actually boarded it...

03:22.640 --> 03:24.010
That's right.

03:24.350 --> 03:28.430
The pilot at that time was fully
resonating with the module.

03:28.430 --> 03:31.600
And yet the results were highly disappointing.

03:31.600 --> 03:37.480
We'd like to be very cautious this time so
that we don't make the same mistake again.

03:42.530 --> 03:44.160
That was good. Very good.

03:44.160 --> 03:46.160
That was a great counterargument.

03:46.160 --> 03:49.160
The Shirogane's failure is traumatic to those officials.

03:51.040 --> 03:56.710
In order to prevent further Gargouille casualties, we need to be careful.

03:56.710 --> 03:58.500
Is that what I am to assume?

04:01.340 --> 04:02.680
If you'll excuse me.

04:10.930 --> 04:14.560
The Argent is nothing like the Shirogane.

04:14.560 --> 04:16.770
It has an LIM on board.

04:16.770 --> 04:17.730
Right? Right? Right?

04:27.530 --> 04:28.620
As you can see,

04:28.620 --> 04:34.120
this MA-Vess's design is based on the Argent and is the second prototype.

04:34.120 --> 04:37.290
And one of us will be piloting it, of course.

04:38.090 --> 04:39.210
That's right.

04:41.010 --> 04:41.920
It's fine.

04:43.590 --> 04:44.930
I'll pilot it.

04:45.260 --> 04:49.140
You're already synced with the Argent.

04:49.140 --> 04:51.640
You won't be piloting this one.

04:54.810 --> 04:56.400
<i>He</i>'s not here?

04:56.810 --> 05:01.400
If you mean Isaku Heito,
he's been AWOL for a few days now.

05:01.400 --> 05:04.530
Wouldn't that count as mismanagement on your part?

05:05.030 --> 05:08.490
Management of his behavior is not part of my duties.

05:10.280 --> 05:11.580
Oh well...

05:11.580 --> 05:14.000
Would you like to test them one by one?

05:16.500 --> 05:18.000
I'll pilot it.

05:18.000 --> 05:19.460
What about your arm?

05:20.090 --> 05:22.920
I don't want to be treated like a cripple forever.

05:23.920 --> 05:25.630
Then go right on ahead.

05:32.430 --> 05:34.060
Connecting to LIM.

05:35.310 --> 05:37.310
Filters at 95%.

05:37.310 --> 05:37.810
Connecting...

05:53.950 --> 05:55.370
Raika! Raika?!

05:55.370 --> 05:56.710
Disconnecting!

06:00.250 --> 06:02.090
Get her out of the cockpit!

06:02.090 --> 06:03.050
Hurry!

06:05.460 --> 06:07.170
You all right?

06:07.170 --> 06:08.380
Thanks.

06:09.050 --> 06:14.180
Akashi was saying it feels like someone's poking around inside your head.

06:14.770 --> 06:17.390
I don't think I even got there.

06:18.020 --> 06:21.150
I had goosebumps the instant it booted up.

06:21.150 --> 06:23.400
I don't think I even lasted a minute.

06:23.400 --> 06:24.530
How pathetic.

06:25.820 --> 06:27.450
Pathetic or not...

06:27.450 --> 06:29.320
That isn't the issue, is it?

06:30.160 --> 06:31.910
What do you mean?

06:31.910 --> 06:33.280
Well...

06:33.280 --> 06:38.410
No matter how you look at it,
I think the problem is with that MA-Vess.

06:39.290 --> 06:43.040
It's way too creepy for <i>just</i> a machine.

06:45.760 --> 06:47.300
What's the matter?

06:48.340 --> 06:52.180
I thought about reporting why
the connection test was a failure.

06:52.180 --> 06:55.850
That reaction was instinctive hatred upon connection.

06:55.850 --> 06:58.680
Nothing more, nothing less.

07:00.730 --> 07:04.480
Was there something unreasonable about the LIM theory after all?

07:05.940 --> 07:07.570
That's not it.

07:07.570 --> 07:10.740
I knew Raika Kasumi wouldn't cut it from the start.

07:10.740 --> 07:13.200
Her compatibility was very low too.

07:13.200 --> 07:16.950
We shouldn't have repeated such an unreasonable act.

07:17.910 --> 07:19.710
You're saying that now?

07:19.710 --> 07:22.120
It was what the other side wished for.

07:22.120 --> 07:24.130
That's just an excuse!

07:25.540 --> 07:27.300
What?

07:27.300 --> 07:28.880
Are you criticizing me?

07:32.840 --> 07:34.180
What about you?!

07:35.390 --> 07:40.230
When we customized the Shirogane, I told you anything and everything!

07:40.230 --> 07:43.900
And you accepted it!
You're the one who told me to do it!

07:43.900 --> 07:45.150
Am I wrong?

07:45.150 --> 07:46.400
That's...

07:46.400 --> 07:51.820
Back then, I just didn't want to lose, no matter how it ended up.

07:51.820 --> 07:52.660
However...

07:54.660 --> 07:57.240
I don't want your criticism!

07:57.620 --> 07:59.750
No criticism! No criticism!

08:05.000 --> 08:08.800
In the end, Raika hopped on and we got dismissed.

08:09.260 --> 08:11.720
We have no idea what they're thinking.

08:16.800 --> 08:18.310
I'll go on ahead.

08:20.270 --> 08:21.770
H-Hey!

08:29.900 --> 08:31.150
Akashi-kun...

08:31.150 --> 08:32.450
Something on your mind?

08:34.740 --> 08:36.620
Like the Corpse and whatnot.

08:39.330 --> 08:40.870
How should I put it...

08:40.870 --> 08:43.120
I thought you'd be shocked or something.

08:44.750 --> 08:46.880
I met it in my dream.

08:47.920 --> 08:49.130
I see.

08:50.460 --> 08:52.470
You said that before.

08:55.260 --> 08:59.970
I didn't tell anyone until now,
but I had dreams like that too.

09:01.470 --> 09:03.140
Dreams that a Corpse showed up.

09:11.860 --> 09:15.530
Hey! Where are you?

09:16.660 --> 09:18.370
Where?

09:18.370 --> 09:20.200
Where did they go?

09:26.830 --> 09:27.750
Akashi...

09:29.340 --> 09:29.960
Akashi...

09:34.510 --> 09:35.930
No!

09:51.230 --> 09:52.480
Akashi...

09:57.860 --> 09:59.280
It's strange.

09:59.570 --> 10:01.620
Like Iwato and Raika,

10:01.620 --> 10:04.540
everyone else around me looked like kid versions of themselves.

10:05.660 --> 10:08.710
It was a dream I kept having since before I met everyone.

10:10.840 --> 10:16.510
And in that dream, I was searching for someone.

10:18.550 --> 10:20.220
That person was you.

10:21.100 --> 10:22.140
Really?

10:22.850 --> 10:24.060
Yeah.

10:24.060 --> 10:26.230
That's what I felt when I first met you.

10:28.190 --> 10:29.650
Was it really me?

10:33.820 --> 10:35.730
Oh, sorry...

10:36.490 --> 10:37.280
Sasame...

10:37.280 --> 10:38.780
I'll be going now.

10:43.700 --> 10:44.870
Sasame...

11:03.970 --> 11:05.180
It's tough, isn't it?

11:14.190 --> 11:15.770
So crumpled...

11:15.770 --> 11:16.690
I'm sorry.

11:17.990 --> 11:21.860
I'm connected the most with you, Sasame.

11:24.410 --> 11:29.080
I had started to think that being connected was more fun.

11:30.920 --> 11:34.040
But for now, I'm still scared.

11:34.040 --> 11:35.750
I don't want them to know.

11:37.300 --> 11:39.510
How did we end up like this?

11:40.630 --> 11:41.470
Actually...

11:43.720 --> 11:45.140
you should have a memory of it.

11:45.800 --> 11:46.810
Even you, Sasame.

11:47.850 --> 11:48.770
Minashi...

12:05.620 --> 12:06.870
You're not gone...

12:08.370 --> 12:10.000
You're not gone, right?

12:10.870 --> 12:12.290
Answer me,

12:14.040 --> 12:16.090
my terror.

12:16.920 --> 12:18.460
All right. Next person's turn.

12:28.970 --> 12:29.600
Thanks.

12:29.600 --> 12:30.930
I'm okay.

12:34.730 --> 12:36.400
Sasame!

12:54.330 --> 12:55.920
It's Kasane-san...

13:18.150 --> 13:21.150
This area is completely in ruins now.

13:30.450 --> 13:34.540
You weren't the one who called
me all the way out here, were you?

13:35.330 --> 13:36.000
Heito...

13:36.290 --> 13:37.790
False alarm.

13:37.790 --> 13:40.290
I figured as much too.

13:41.340 --> 13:45.300
There's no reason for you to call me out to have a chat.

13:45.300 --> 13:47.050
What's this about?

13:47.050 --> 13:52.510
There's someone out there who wanted the two of us to meet face to face!

13:54.350 --> 13:55.230
Kasane?

13:55.230 --> 13:57.020
Give it back!

13:57.020 --> 13:58.770
Kasane is that old hag?

13:59.060 --> 14:01.020
Did she plan this?

14:01.020 --> 14:02.360
Who knows?

14:03.900 --> 14:09.200
And you came yippin' along, waggin' your tail,
and doing as you're told so that you could get laid.

14:10.490 --> 14:14.830
It's nice around here 'cause there's lots
of rooms that serve in place of love hotels.

14:16.500 --> 14:18.920
"Defeat the Corpse, Akashi!"

14:19.370 --> 14:22.920
She was seeking salvation from you all along,

14:22.920 --> 14:26.970
yet your head is filled with nothing but that old hag.

14:26.970 --> 14:29.130
You're so cold.

14:29.890 --> 14:31.300
You talking about Emiru?

14:31.760 --> 14:35.430
Oh, so you have enough guilt in
you to understand at least that much.

14:37.100 --> 14:37.140
Playing with
balls is forbidden!

14:37.100 --> 14:37.140
Kuhicho
Neighborhood Association

14:37.140 --> 14:37.180
Playing with
balls is forbidden!

14:46.030 --> 14:47.690
Don't get me wrong.

14:49.070 --> 14:51.240
I appreciate what you did.

14:52.030 --> 14:59.870
Because you abandoned her, she sunk
deeper and deeper into terror all alone.

15:02.290 --> 15:03.790
My Emiru!

15:03.790 --> 15:05.670
She was the best.

15:05.670 --> 15:09.760
Whenever I went into her heart,
she would coldly reject me.

15:10.130 --> 15:16.310
So every time I had the chance, I'd torment
her more and more, and she'd tremble in fear.

15:16.310 --> 15:17.980
It was the best...

15:18.430 --> 15:21.980
What the hell kind of terrible things did you do to her?!

15:21.980 --> 15:23.480
Playing with
balls is forbidden!

15:21.980 --> 15:24.270
Terrible?

15:24.270 --> 15:25.320
You make me laugh.

15:26.020 --> 15:29.320
You're the type of person that's most vicious, don't you think?

15:30.450 --> 15:35.280
Downright cold-hearted, yet you act just
a bit nice, as if you were making an excuse.

15:37.080 --> 15:41.000
In other words, you don't want to cross
that one line that makes you a good person.

15:42.330 --> 15:45.590
Guys like that tend to betray
others at the last possible second.

15:45.960 --> 15:47.050
You don't recall?

15:47.050 --> 15:50.170
Didn't you make multiple people cry?

15:51.340 --> 15:52.680
Is it really me?

15:56.930 --> 15:59.060
Poor Emiru!

15:59.060 --> 16:01.850
Being played around by someone like this!

16:02.980 --> 16:04.480
"I don't want to die.

16:04.480 --> 16:06.360
Defeat it for me, Akashi."

16:05.440 --> 16:06.360
Shut up.

16:06.900 --> 16:08.110
"I don't want to die.

16:08.440 --> 16:11.110
Defeat the Corpse, Akashi.

16:11.110 --> 16:13.070
Akashi!"

16:15.780 --> 16:19.240
"I'm scared, Akashi."

16:17.120 --> 16:17.660
Shut up...

16:20.620 --> 16:21.580
Shut the fuck up!

16:39.140 --> 16:40.600
Here I come!

16:42.770 --> 16:43.890
Next!

16:43.890 --> 16:44.940
Come on!

16:53.820 --> 16:58.160
How about<i> you</i> cry a bit for a change?

17:10.670 --> 17:12.050
You're still here?

17:12.420 --> 17:14.010
Would you like to watch too?

17:15.090 --> 17:16.970
What are you watching?

17:16.970 --> 17:18.800
Sorry in advance.

17:18.800 --> 17:22.930
I enticed Saginuma-kun out by using your name.

17:23.230 --> 17:26.400
With the excuse you'd tell him the Argent's secrets.

17:27.560 --> 17:28.860
For what reason?

17:28.860 --> 17:34.150
To rouse number two from its slumber, with Isaku Heito in the cockpit.

17:34.150 --> 17:39.830
Heito followed suit too after reading the note
that told him he could find out where Emiru is.

17:39.830 --> 17:41.290
Why Akashi, though?

17:41.580 --> 17:44.450
Well, just watch for a while.

17:44.450 --> 17:46.290
Observation is the most basic principle.

17:46.290 --> 17:48.750
I'm seeing all sorts of things already.

17:49.790 --> 17:52.210
Including the delicate balance between the three.

17:53.130 --> 17:54.170
The three?

18:03.680 --> 18:05.640
What the hell's his problem?

18:09.400 --> 18:10.520
Someone's calling...

18:10.520 --> 18:11.690
Who is it?

18:22.870 --> 18:24.040
The Reaper.

18:24.040 --> 18:25.500
No, something else.

18:25.500 --> 18:26.620
This is...

18:29.000 --> 18:29.960
Oh crap...

18:31.000 --> 18:32.420
You found it.

18:32.750 --> 18:34.050
That's right.

18:34.050 --> 18:36.010
You're attracted to each other.

18:49.060 --> 18:50.310
Are you here?

18:52.440 --> 18:53.820
That's right. Hop on!

18:53.820 --> 18:56.820
What you seek lies inside it.

18:58.030 --> 18:58.900
He's getting in!

19:28.640 --> 19:29.940
I felt her.

19:29.940 --> 19:33.730
I felt her rejecting me just now.

19:34.110 --> 19:35.440
Watch the data!

19:35.440 --> 19:36.940
The LIM must've booted too!

19:36.940 --> 19:37.570
Right!

19:37.860 --> 19:39.820
It's just as I thought.

19:39.820 --> 19:44.320
That kid had an awakening
the very first time on the Argent.

19:44.320 --> 19:45.410
Give me data!

19:45.410 --> 19:46.540
It's not moving.

19:47.160 --> 19:48.370
What?

19:48.370 --> 19:50.160
The LIM hasn't booted up!

19:51.210 --> 19:52.170
Why?

19:52.170 --> 19:55.210
There's no mistake with this pairing!

20:00.800 --> 20:01.590
Akashi!

20:09.810 --> 20:11.180
Akashi!

20:22.860 --> 20:24.950
Tremble in fear! Feel the terror!

20:35.170 --> 20:36.880
Here I come!

20:51.680 --> 20:56.150
If I killed Akashi, would you reject me again?

21:01.280 --> 21:01.990
What is that?

21:03.780 --> 21:05.410
Akashi...

21:05.700 --> 21:07.200
The LIM booted up...

21:08.160 --> 21:09.120
Yes!

21:30.350 --> 21:31.970
Good, good...

21:31.970 --> 21:34.310
You have high specs like I thought.

21:35.890 --> 21:40.400
Akashi's existence served perfectly as the catalyst.

21:40.400 --> 21:43.990
It was worth the effort of luring
him all the way out there as well!

21:45.740 --> 21:47.700
What in the world is going on?

21:48.410 --> 21:52.660
As you can see, the second machine, Sable, has awoken.

22:03.880 --> 22:05.340
What?

22:05.340 --> 22:09.140
He was that cold to you, but it still has to be Akashi?

22:09.140 --> 22:11.930
You came all the way out to save him, huh?

22:13.430 --> 22:14.720
That's fine by me.

22:14.720 --> 22:17.890
Thank you for coming back.

22:17.890 --> 22:19.520
Now I can be one

22:20.560 --> 22:22.520
with the terror once again.

22:25.530 --> 22:31.990
So please don't go away ever again, my terror.

22:44.800 --> 22:55.430
Throwing away all my excuses, I traced over my abrased heart

22:55.430 --> 22:59.980
In the coldness of the locker room,

22:59.980 --> 23:06.440
Was an unfulfilled promise, locked away

23:06.940 --> 23:12.910
Dispel the darkness in this fallen world,

23:12.910 --> 23:17.450
And give me a reason why I should continue living

23:17.450 --> 23:22.830
The meaning of good-byes, the expectations of people,

23:22.830 --> 23:27.710
And the melodies that we played while never crossing paths

23:27.710 --> 23:33.430
I know I must not run away. The only path is straight ahead

23:33.430 --> 23:37.930
Even if this turns out to be a mistake

23:37.930 --> 23:43.520
The whirlpools of destiny will consume all loneliness

23:43.520 --> 23:51.610
It is an unerasable scar, an egoism that cannot be discarded

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Episode 8

24:05.000 --> 24:10.010
Reckless Forbidden Realm
